.TH R_MEMPOOL_FREE_ENTRY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
r_mempool_free_entry \- free an entry back to the ranged pool
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

r_mempool_free_entry(entry);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns an allocated entry to the appropriate sub-pool's free list.
Macro wrapper around mempool_free_entry() that sets pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
entry  Entry to free (will be set to NULL after freeing)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Works for entries from any sub-pool in the ranged pool
Also works for dynamically allocated entries (fallback)
Safe to call with NULL
Thread-safe if pool created with single_threaded=false
Performs corruption detection via assertions
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR mempool_free_entry (3),
.BR r_mempool_alloc_entry (3)
